    "created_at": "2016-09-28T10:59:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-28T10:59:05Z",
    "body": "> I think you forgot to update the element and attribute indexes? \n\nAre those not autogenerated? Bleh.\n\n> Looks okay otherwise, although I'm a little worried about link element fetching mismatching with implementations still. I suspect there is some branching going on, but always passing along nonce doesn't seem bad.\n\nChrome only uses `nonce` attributes on `<link>` for stylesheets; I don't think we have a particular interest in applying nonces to other request types at the moment. But, as you say, it does no harm, and wiring things up to allow CSP to make a decision seems reasonable.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
